{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review & reform Corporation Tax Quarterly Instalment Payment thresholds & rules",
        "additional_details": "The \u00a31.5m threshold has remained unchanged since its intro almost 30 years ago. Businesses can be treated as \"large\" even when their profits are modest, because the threshold is divided by the number of associated companies, regardless of the profits of each company. Companies must also estimate profits months before year-end and can be charged interest if forecasts prove wrong. Businesses should pay the correct tax, but should not be penalised for failing to predict future events.",
        "background": "Review and reform Corporation Tax Quarterly Instalment Payment rules:\r\n- Increase the outdated \u00a31.5m threshold\r\n- Change associated-company rules so they are based on economic reality\r\n- Abolish interest charges based on profits that could not reasonably have been predicted when payments became due",
